WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.295
Lesson 12.3.

00:00:02.295 --> 00:00:05.230
The credit line: borrowing like a bank client.

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:07.261
By the end of this lesson, you'll be

00:00:07.261 --> 00:00:09.566
able to use your assets as collateral for

00:00:09.566 --> 00:00:12.695
liquidity without selling, under a written credit policy.

00:00:13.995 --> 00:00:15.285
Here's the plan.

00:00:15.285 --> 00:00:16.970
First, the key ideas.

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:19.685
Then, a worked example, step by step.

00:00:19.685 --> 00:00:21.210
Then, your checklist.

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:23.372
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:24.672 --> 00:00:27.810
Wealthy clients rarely sell appreciating assets to

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:30.387
raise cash; they borrow against them.

00:00:30.387 --> 00:00:33.200
DeFi money markets offer the same: deposit

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:36.601
collateral, borrow stablecoins, repay when it suits

00:00:36.601 --> 00:00:38.602
you, with no credit check.

00:00:38.602 --> 00:00:41.023
The collateral is liquidated if you breach

00:00:41.023 --> 00:00:43.462
the threshold, and nobody calls first.

00:00:43.462 --> 00:00:48.701
A credit policy (write yours): First, Max LTV 25–30%

00:00:48.701 --> 00:00:54.537
on volatile collateral (liquidation is often near 80%+).

00:00:54.537 --> 00:00:58.742
Next, Health factor floor 2.5; act at 2.0.

00:00:58.742 --> 00:01:01.368
Then, Prefer collateral whose yield

00:01:01.368 --> 00:01:04.222
covers the interest (strategy #25).

00:01:04.222 --> 00:01:07.566
Also, Consider fixed-rate borrowing when a rate

00:01:07.566 --> 00:01:10.652
spike would force a sale (strategy #22).

00:01:10.652 --> 00:01:13.236
On top of that, Repayment source named

00:01:13.236 --> 00:01:16.417
before borrowing (income, reserve, maturing PT).

00:01:17.718 --> 00:01:20.485
And finally, Tax treatment of borrowing varies

00:01:20.485 --> 00:01:22.958
by country: check with a tax professional.

00:01:24.258 --> 00:01:26.773
Let's work an example, step by step.

00:01:26.773 --> 00:01:34.898
$200,000 of liquid-staked ETH earning 3.2% ($6,400 a year).

00:01:34.898 --> 00:01:40.553
Borrow $40,000 stablecoins at 5% ($2,000 a year).

00:01:40.553 --> 00:01:43.358
Yield covers interest 3.2 times .

00:01:43.358 --> 00:01:45.463
L.T.V.

00:01:45.463 --> 00:01:49.378
20%. health factor 4.0 at a 0.8 threshold.

00:01:49.378 --> 00:01:52.401
ETH would have to fall about 75% before

00:01:52.401 --> 00:01:57.008
liquidation (health factor falls in proportion to price).

00:01:57.008 --> 00:02:00.353
Defence plan: at health factor 2.0, repay from

00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:03.484
reserve; at health factor 1.7, sell part of

00:02:03.484 --> 00:02:07.541
the collateral deliberately rather than let a liquidator

00:02:07.541 --> 00:02:08.893
do it at a penalty.

00:02:10.193 --> 00:02:11.653
Here's your checklist.

00:02:11.653 --> 00:02:13.188
Do it now, for real.

00:02:13.188 --> 00:02:16.070
First, Credit policy written: max

00:02:16.070 --> 00:02:18.829
LTV, HF floor, action levels.

00:02:18.829 --> 00:02:20.794
Next, Repayment source named.

00:02:20.794 --> 00:02:25.109
Then, Alerts set at the action levels (Module 14.1).

00:02:25.109 --> 00:02:28.799
And finally, Fixed vs variable decision made on purpose.

00:02:30.099 --> 00:02:31.309
Question 1.

00:02:31.309 --> 00:02:33.934
Why borrow against assets instead of selling them?

00:02:38.354 --> 00:02:41.342
The answer: You keep the asset and its upside

00:02:41.342 --> 00:02:44.785
(and in some jurisdictions avoid a taxable sale), at

00:02:44.785 --> 00:02:47.514
the cost of interest and liquidation risk.

00:02:48.814 --> 00:02:50.059
Question 2.

00:02:50.059 --> 00:02:52.384
HF is 4.0.

00:02:52.384 --> 00:02:55.599
Roughly how far can collateral fall before liquidation?

00:03:00.019 --> 00:03:03.499
The answer: About 75%, since HF scales

00:03:03.499 --> 00:03:06.622
with collateral price (HF 1.0 at a

00:03:06.622 --> 00:03:09.299
quarter of the current price).

00:03:10.599 --> 00:03:11.869
Question 3.

00:03:11.869 --> 00:03:13.594
What should happen at your action level?

00:03:18.014 --> 00:03:19.435
The answer: Repay or add

00:03:19.435 --> 00:03:21.554
collateral per the written plan.

00:03:21.554 --> 00:03:23.686
Sell deliberately before a liquidator

00:03:23.686 --> 00:03:24.864
does it at a penalty.

00:03:26.164 --> 00:03:27.409
Let's recap.

00:03:27.409 --> 00:03:31.736
Max LTV 25–30% on volatile collateral

00:03:31.736 --> 00:03:35.794
(liquidation is often near 80%+).

00:03:35.794 --> 00:03:39.689
Health factor floor 2.5: act at 2.0.

00:03:39.689 --> 00:03:44.699
Prefer collateral whose yield covers the interest (strategy #25).

00:03:44.699 --> 00:03:47.880
Consider fixed-rate borrowing when a rate spike

00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:50.134
would force a sale (strategy #22).

00:03:51.434 --> 00:03:53.949
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:03:53.949 --> 00:03:57.894
Next up, Lesson 12.4: Treasury and the liquidity ladder.
